We want to find $(x+1)^{48}$.
We can rewrite $x$ as:
$x = \frac{4}{(\sqrt{5}+1)(\sqrt[4]{5}+1)(\sqrt[8]{5}+1)(\sqrt[16]{5}+1)}$

Let $a = \sqrt{5}$, $b = \sqrt[4]{5}$, $c = \sqrt[8]{5}$, $d = \sqrt[16]{5}$.
Then $x = \frac{4}{(a+1)(b+1)(c+1)(d+1)}$.
Note that $(a+1)(b+1) = ab + a + b + 1$.
We have
$(a+1)(b+1)(c+1)(d+1) = \left(ab + a + b + 1\right)(c+1)(d+1)$
