Let $A = \begin{pmatrix} \sec^2 x & 1 & 1 \\ \cos^2 x & \cos^2 x & \csc^2 x \\ 1 & \cos^2 x & \cot^2 x \end{pmatrix}$. We want to find $\det(A)$.

We expand the determinant along the first row:
\begin{align*} \det(A) &= \sec^2 x \begin{vmatrix} \cos^2 x & \csc^2 x \\ \cos^2 x & \cot^2 x \end{vmatrix} - 1 \begin{vmatrix} \cos^2 x & \csc^2 x \\ 1 & \cot^2 x \end{vmatrix} + 1 \begin{vmatrix} \cos^2 x & \cos^2 x \\ 1 & \cos^2 x \end{vmatrix} \\ &= \sec^2 x (\cos^2 x \cot^2 x - \csc^2 x \cos^2 x) - (\cos^2 x \cot^2 x - \csc^2 x) + (\cos^4 x - \cos^2 x) \\ &= \sec^2 x \cos^2 x (\cot^2 x - \csc^2 x) - \cos^2 x \cot^2 x + \csc^2 x + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{1}{\cos^2 x} \cos^2 x \left( \frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} - \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} \right) - \cos^2 x \frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} + \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \left( \frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} - \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} \right) - \frac{\cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} + \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{\cos^2 x - 1}{\sin^2 x} - \frac{\cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} + \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{\cos^2 x - 1 + 1 - \cos^4 x + \sin^2 x}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{\sin^2 x - \cos^4 x + \cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{\sin^2 x - \cos^4 x + \cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \end{align*}

However, we can simplify this as follows:
\begin{align*} \det(A) &= \sec^2 x (\cos^2 x \cot^2 x - \csc^2 x \cos^2 x) - (\cos^2 x \cot^2 x - \csc^2 x) + (\cos^4 x - \cos^2 x) \\ &= \sec^2 x (\cos^2 x \frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} - \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} \cos^2 x) - (\cos^2 x \frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} - \frac{1}{\sin^2 x}) + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \sec^2 x (\frac{\cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} - \frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x}) - \frac{\cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} + \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{1}{\cos^2 x} (\frac{\cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} - \frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x}) - \frac{\cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} + \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{\cos^4 x - \cos^2 x}{\cos^2 x \sin^2 x} - \frac{\cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} + \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{\cos^4 x - \cos^2 x}{\cos^2 x \sin^2 x} - \frac{\cos^4 x \cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x \cos^2 x} + \frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{\cos^4 x - \cos^2 x}{\cos^2 x \sin^2 x} - \frac{\cos^6 x}{\cos^2 x \sin^2 x} + \frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{\cos^4 x - \cos^2 x - \cos^6 x + \cos^2 x \sin^2 x}{\cos^2 x \sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \end{align*} 
Alternatively, we can use $\cot^2 x = \csc^2 x - 1$.
Then
\begin{align*} \det(A) &= \sec^2 x(\cos^2 x (\csc^2 x - 1) - \csc^2 x \cos^2 x) - (\cos^2 x (\csc^2 x - 1) - \csc^2 x) + (\cos^4 x - \cos^2 x) \\ &= \sec^2 x(\cos^2 x \csc^2 x - \cos^2 x - \csc^2 x \cos^2 x) - (\cos^2 x \csc^2 x - \cos^2 x - \csc^2 x) + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{1}{\cos^2 x} (\cos^2 x \csc^2 x - \cos^2 x - \csc^2 x \cos^2 x) - \cos^2 x \csc^2 x + \cos^2 x + \csc^2 x + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{\cos^2 x \csc^2 x - \cos^2 x - \csc^2 x \cos^2 x}{\cos^2 x} - \cos^2 x \csc^2 x + \csc^2 x + \cos^4 x \\ &= \cos^2 x \csc^2 x - \cos^2 x - \csc^2 x \cos^2 x - \cos^2 x \csc^2 x + \csc^2 x + \cos^4 x \\ &= - \cos^2 x - \csc^2 x \cos^2 x + \csc^2 x + \cos^4 x \\ &= \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x + \csc^2 x (1 - \cos^2 x) \\ &= \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x + \csc^2 x \sin^2 x \\ &= \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x + \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} \sin^2 x \\ &= \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x + 1 \end{align*} 
If $x = \frac{\pi}{4}$, we have $\cos x = \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}$ and $\sin x = \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}$. Then
$$ \det(A) = \left( \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}} \right)^4 - \left( \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}} \right)^2 + 1 = \frac{1}{4} - \frac{1}{2} + 1 = \frac{1}{4} - \frac{2}{4} + \frac{4}{4} = \frac{3}{4} $$
Final Answer: The final answer is $\boxed{3/4}$
