The width of the pool is $6\text{ m}$, the length is $12\text{ m}$, and the depth is $4\text{ m}$.
Since the pool is half full, the height of the water is $\frac{1}{2} \times 4\text{ m} = 2\text{ m}$.

The volume of water in the pool is $6 \text{ m} \times 12 \text{ m} \times 2\text{ m} = (6 \times 12 \times 2) \text{ m}^3 = (72 \times 2) \text{ m}^3 = 144 \text{ m}^3$.

\boxed{144 \text{ m}^3}
