Since $\sin x,$ $\cos x,$ $\tan x$ form a geometric sequence, we have $\frac{\cos x}{\sin x} = \frac{\tan x}{\cos x},$ so $\cos^2 x = \sin x \tan x.$  This gives us $\cos^2 x = \sin x \cdot \frac{\sin x}{\cos x} = \frac{\sin^2 x}{\cos x},$ so $\cos^3 x = \sin^2 x.$  Therefore,
\begin{align*} \cos^3 x + \cos^2 x &= \sin^2 x + \cos^2 x \\ &= 1. \end{align*}

Thus,
\[ \cos^3 x + \cos^2 x = 1. \]
In this case, the answer is 1, so the units are none. 
