Here's the solution to the problem:

\textbf{Step 1:}
The total number of possible assignments of the 4 papers to the 4 students is the number of permutations of 4 items, which is $4! = 4 \times 3 \times 2 \times 1 = 24$.

\textbf{Step 2:}
The teacher randomly guesses. This means each student has an equal chance of being assigned each of the 4 papers. The teacher guesses the papers for each of the four students. The number of ways to assign 4 distinct papers to 4 distinct students is $4! = 4 \times 3 \times 2 \times 1 = 24$. 

\textbf{Step 3:}
The probability that the teacher correctly guesses the paper for each of the four students is the number of ways to assign the papers correctly (which is 1) divided by the total number of possible assignments (which is $4! = 24$). Thus, the probability is $\frac{1}{24}$.

