Expanding the right side, we get
$x^4-3x^3+4x^2+11x-9 = x^4 + ax^3 + bx^2 - 3x^3 - 3ax^2 - 3bx + 2x^2 + 2ax + 2b + cx + d$
$x^4-3x^3+4x^2+11x-9 = x^4 + (a-3)x^3 + (b-3a+2)x^2 + (-3b+2a+c)x + (2b+d)$
Comparing coefficients, we have
$a-3 = -3 \implies a = 0$
$b-3a+2 = 4 \implies b-0+2 = 4 \implies b = 2$
$-3b+2a+c = 11 \implies -3(2)+0+c = 11 \implies -6+c = 11 \implies c = 17$
$2b+d = -9 \implies 2(2)+d = -9 \implies 4+d = -9 \implies d = -13$
The remainder is $cx+d = 17x - 13$.

