    \item Therefore, $f(x) = -f(x)$. This implies that $2f(x) = 0$, so $f(x) = 0$ for all $x$.
    \item Thus, the only function that is both even and odd is the zero function, i.e., $f(x) = 0$.
    \item Therefore, there is only 1 function that is both even and odd.
\end{enumerate}

